.\"  mypm.1 - manual page for mypm (Truck package manager, trk)
.\"  Part of Asombi OS <https://github.com/WFStudio-app/Asombi>
.\"
.TH MYPN 1 "mypm" "October 2026" "Asombi OS 0.2.00" "Asombi OS User Manuals"
.SH NAME
mypm \- package manager for Asombi OS (alias of
.BR trk ,
the Truck Package Manager)
.ad left
.hy 0
.nh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mypm
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mypm
is the package-management front-end of Asombi OS. It installs, removes,
updates and audits binary packages built from sources into lightweight
Alpine-based instances. The command set is identical to
.BR trk (1);
.B mypm
exists as a convenience alias so users can type their package manager in
their own words.
.PP
Packages are described by TOML manifests and resolved from one or more
repositories (see
.BR mypm\ repo ).
Installation compiles binaries inside the instance rootfs and links them
into PATH unless
.B \-\-no-build
is given.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "install " "package[@version] [package2 ...] [\-\-no\-build]"
Install one or more packages. Append
.B @version
to pin a specific release. With
.B \-\-no\-build
only fetch metadata and skip compilation.
.TP
.BI "remove " package
Remove an installed package and unlink its binaries from PATH.
.TP
.BI "update " [package]
Update the given package, or every installed package when no argument
is supplied.
.TP
.BI "search " query
Search all configured repositories for packages matching
.IR query .
Installed packages are marked with
.BR [installed] .
.TP
.B list
List installed packages together with their versions.
.TP
.BI "info " package
Show detailed information about a package: version, description,
dependencies, source URL and install state.
.TP
.BI "link " package
Re-link the built binaries of an already installed package into PATH
(useful after a manual cleanup).
.TP
.BI "repo add " url
Register an additional package repository.
.TP
.BI "repo remove " url
Deregister a repository.
.TP
.BI "repo list"
List all configured repositories.
.TP
.B clean
Clear the download and build cache.
.TP
.B version
Print the Truck/mypm version and exit.
.TP
.BR "help" , "\ " "-h" , "\ " "--help"
Show the usage banner with the command summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-build
Valid for
.BR install ;
skip source compilation and only register the package.
.TP
.B @version
Version-pin syntax valid for
.B install
and
.BR info .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.asombi/instances/
Instance root directories containing per-instance package databases.
.TP
.B ~/.asombi/packages/
Shared package database (installed-package records).
.TP
.B ~/.asombi/cache/
Download and build cache managed by
.BR "mypm clean" .
.TP
.B ~/.asombi/logs/
Build logs for failed compilations.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install ripgrep, compiling from source:
.PP
.EX
$ mypm install ripgrep
.EE
.PP
Install a pinned version without building:
.PP
.EX
$ mypm install neovim@0.9.5 --no-build
.EE
.PP
Add a community repository and search it:
.PP
.EX
$ mypm repo add https://example.com/repo/index.toml
$ mypm search editor
.EE
.PP
Update everything and clean up afterwards:
.PP
.EX
$ mypm update
$ mypm clean
.EE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
On unknown commands
.B mypm
prints
.RB "[trk]\ Unknown\ command:\ ..."
and exits with status
.BR 1 .
If the truck core directory is missing from the installation, it exits
with a hint to re-run
.BR install.sh .
Exit status
.B 0
indicates success.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.nf
.B 0
success
.B 1
invalid usage, unknown command or failed operation
.fi
